messages:
maria_support: Heads up — customer on Vercel Edge reported intermittent 401s mid-stream when using the TypeScript/Node SDK's ReadableStream path. Started after they upgraded SDK from 3.1.4 -> 3.2.1.
kevin_eng: Can you paste the minimal repro (client call + runtime)?
maria_support: Minimal code they shared:```ts
const client = new InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.API_KEY });
const res = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'gpt-open', input: 'hello' });
const reader = res.body.getReader();
while(true){
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if(done) break;
  process.stdout.write(new TextDecoder().decode(value));
}
```
ryan_devex: What Node version and edge runtime? Vercel edge uses V8 isolates — no native fetch token refresh.
maria_support: They said: Node 18 local repro OK, but on Vercel Edge it fails ~30% of the time. Error they see: `TypeError: The user stream closed unexpectedly` and console shows intermittent 401 responses interleaved with chunks.
kevin_eng: Hm. Sounds like the auth retry/backoff flow is attempting to refresh or replay Authorization header mid-stream, but edge runtime disallows a second auth handshake. Any proxy in front?
maria_support: It's direct to our hosted endpoint (no customer proxy). CI deploy logs (ci-bot): `deploy v2.14 -> vercel-edge-us-east` at 2850001099.
kevin_eng: Can we get raw HTTP capture? Ask them to set DEBUG=redwood-inference:stream and include x-request-id from failing stream.
dani_sre: Quick theory: SDK change in 3.2.1 introduced 'adaptive' retry that retries on 401 once with refreshed token. In edge runtimes the refresh path returns a short-lived rotated token which sometimes races with the streaming connection, producing a 401 during an open chunked response. That race closes the ReadableStream in Node and the client observes premature close.
ryan_devex: Workarounds to propose: 1) pin SDK to 3.1.4 (known-good) 2) disable adaptive retry via env INFERENCE_SDK_RETRY=off or set retryMode: 'standard' when constructing client 3) switch to non-edge (serverful) deployment for streaming heavy flows.
maria_support: Customer tried pinning to 3.1.4 and saw stable streams for 24h. They also tested setting retryMode: 'standard' and that also removed mid-stream 401s.
kevin_eng: We'll file a runtime bug: stream-auth-race-edge. Short-term patch: make SDK avoid token-refresh-based retry for streaming requests in edge runtimes (detect env) and fall back to header-preserve/no-retry. Long-term: fix token rotation atomicity server-side.
dani_sre: Added incident tracking note and flagged for Dedicated customers who use token rotation.
ryan_devex: For support reply: include repro steps, required headers (x-request-id), recommended workaround (pin 3.1.4 or set retryMode:'standard'), and ask for debug logs. Also mention we're rolling a patch to disable adaptive auth retry on streaming in edge runtimes. :eyes:
maria_support: Reply sent to customer with instructions and request for logs. Marking thread resolved for now, will update when fix ships. :white_check_mark:
